# Build and tooling artifacts.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Operating system and editor cruft. Nobody else wants these, and .DS_Store in
# particular records what a folder looked like on one person's machine.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Credentials. Nothing that could hold one belongs anywhere near a commit.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Local working notes and assistant instructions. These describe one person's
# machine, folders, and habits. The parts worth publishing live in
# CONTRIBUTING.md; the rest stays local.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.md
.claude/

# Rendered output. Derived from the Markdown sources, which are the versioned
# thing; tracking renders only produces diff noise and version drift.
renders/
# The same documents when someone renders beside the source instead. Anchored
# to the repository root so a font licence or a test fixture is never caught.
/*.pdf
/*.txt
/*.docx

# What the documented quick start writes into a clone: a starter configuration,
# a starter document, and the folder CI's packaging smoke test builds in. None
# of it belongs to the project; it belongs to whoever ran the commands.
/pressume.toml
/reference.docx
/Resume.md
/CV.md
/smoke/
